<!-- RC3 P3 fixture, constructed for GridSim (no third-party content). A 110 kV three-substation network: substation A has
     two busbar sections (CN_A1, CN_A2) joined by a breaker coupler; lines L1 (A1-B) and L2 (A2-B) supply B, L3 (B-C) is
     radial to C. G1 at A1 is the slack (local voltage control, referencePriority 1), G2 at C holds its own voltage, the
     static var compensator at B regulates B. Lines carry permanent (PATL) apparent-power limits; L3 also has a TATL. -->
